 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<table class=\"unnumbered full-width\">\n<thead>\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\"><strong>Dataset C Description</strong></td>\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\"><strong>Data</strong></td>\n\n</tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"left\">Amount of time for a pain reliever to provide relief from migraine headache (time in minutes)</td>\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"left\">Sample of 10 patients: 12.1, 13.8, 9.4, 15.9, 11.5, 14.6, 18.1, 12.7, 11.0, 14.2</td>\n\n</tr></tbody>\n\n</table>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 456335,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "\nFor Dataset C, calculate the range, standard deviation, and variance (round answers to 1 decimal place). \nUse technology as appropriate and include appropriate units as part of your answers.\n\n\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "To find the range, subtract the minimum data value from the maximum data value, which is <span data-math=\"18.1 - \\;9.4 = 8.7\"></span>.<br>\nTo find the standard deviation and variance, use technology as outlined in the following instructions.<br>\nTo use Excel to find the range, standard deviation, and variance, copy the dataset into cells A1 to A10.<br><br>\nTo find the range, in any empty cell, type in:<br>\n=MAX(A1:A10) – MIN(A1:A10)<br><br>\nTo find the standard deviation, in any empty cell, type in: <br>\n=STDEV.S (A1:A10)<br><br>\nTo find the variance, in any empty cell, type in:<br>\n=VAR.S (A1:A10)<br><br>\nTo use Python to find the range, standard deviation, and variance, follow this outline:\n <pre class=\"python\" lang=\"python\"># import the statistics library\nimport statistics\n# define a dataset of 10 numbers\nrelief_times = [12.1, 13.8, 9.4, 15.9, 11.5, 14.6, 18.1, 12.7, 11.0, 14.2]\n# calculate the range of this list using max() and min() functions\nprint(max(relief_times)- min(relief_times))\n# execute the statistics.stdev() function on this list\nprint(statistics.stdev(relief_times))\n# execute the statistics.variance() function on this list\nprint(statistics.variance(relief_times))\n</pre>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\mathrm{Range} = 8.7,\\;\\mathrm{Standard\\;Deviation} = 2.5,\\;\\mathrm{Variance} = 6.5\"></span>\n \n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 456336,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What does the standard deviation of this dataset communicate regarding the amount of time to provide relief from a migraine headache?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "See Solution Manual"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "The standard deviation provides a measure of how far the typical data values are from the mean. In this example, the mean is 13.3 and the standard deviation is 2.5, which indicates a moderate amount of variation in the dataset. The typical average time to obtain relief would extend from 13.3 ± 2.5 minutes."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 456337,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Would a medical researcher prefer to use the standard deviation or the variation for this dataset, and why?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "See Solution Manual "
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "A researcher would prefer to use the standard deviation for this dataset since the units for the standard deviation are in minutes whereas the variance would be measured in square-minutes, which lacks practical significance."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
